    "body": "## Problem\n\nWhen a command emits a message while previous expanded message is still visible, the message is routed to the pager and the pager get focused without explicit user request. Next keys operate in the pager while user still think they are in the buffer window. Docs only mention `g<` as the way to show/enter the pager.\n\nFix #41061\n\n## Solution\n\n- Open the pager without entering it, unless it was explicitly requested (`g<`, `:messages`, or entered from the expanded cmdline).\n- Unfocused pager is kept open while in the cmdline (messages emitted by the entered command are appended to it), entered with `g<`, and dismissed on any other typed key (`q` is consumed so it doesn't start recording a macro).\n",
    "closed_at": null,
