        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Leaning to @justinmk steering, I rework this to reuse existing `cmd_on_key` instead of adding parallel handler. `pager_on_key` is gone now — `messages.lua` diff become 28 lines instead of 76.\n\n- `pager_focus` is only set by explicit request (`g<`, `:messages`, enter from expanded cmdline); `set_pos()` enter the pager only for that.\n- Dismissing of never-entered pager is handled by `cmd_on_key`, which already keep it open while in cmdline and enter on `g<`.\n- One more fix is needed on the way: `cmd_on_key` was also dismiss on **non-typed** keys. The pager own cursor positioning (`win_execute(pager, 'norm! gg0')`) set the `typed_g` latch, so next non-typed key hide the pager immediately. Guarding `typed == ''` is what #39221 want too.\n\n`q` is not special-cased anymore: master leave the same pending-register state for expanded cmdline, so now the pager just follow it.\n",
